{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('../state.json'))\ncur=[i for i in st['interpretations'] if i.get('id')=='e0304928ad0948bba8c4bfd9296712c9-interpretation-0'][0]\nREP=\\\"2f645950e0334342b1f7392ed1c1f286\\\"; ORIG=\\\"01617c5662f34c3eb21857602f6cac4f\\\"\nce=[c for c in cur['counterevidence'] if not c.startswith('Only three of the six trials')]\nce.append(\\\"The split between success and leadership loss varies between executions of the same probe: the first run returned success in three of six trials and leadership loss in the other three, while the repeat returned success in five of six (only the 250ms reconnection answered leadership loss). Across both runs eight of twelve trials returned success, and the successor overlap held in all twelve, so the overlap is what reproduces while the verdict remains a per-trial choice.\\\")\nlim=[l for l in cur['limitations'] if not l.startswith('The stall is a wrapper')]\nlim.insert(0,\\\"The witness rests on two executions of the same fixed probe (receipts 01617c5662f34c3eb21857602f6cac4f and 2f645950e0334342b1f7392ed1c1f286), twelve trials in total, of which eight returned success; the probe is not repeated under different timeouts or stall lengths.\\\")\nlim.append(\\\"The stall is a wrapper around the log store that blocks StoreLogs on the leader's main thread, and the non-voter is reconnected by transport calls; both are supplied conditions rather than faults observed in a deployment.\\\")\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"3b823834c8cb46da98e77d8e988bf5d9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n \\\"executions\\\":{**cur['executions'], REP:[1,3,5,7,9,11]},\n \\\"conclusion\\\":cur['conclusion'],\\\"defect_claim\\\":cur['defect_claim'],\n \\\"rationale\\\":(cur['rationale']+\\\" \\\"\n  \\\"The repeat of that probe strengthens the witness rather than merely confirming it: in the second run (receipt 2f645950e0334342b1f7392ed1c1f286, result events at parsed indices 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11) the successor overlap again appeared in all six trials, with a different server first sampled in Leader state at term 3 between 345ms and 511ms while the old leader stayed at term 2, and five of the six trials returned VerifyLeader success at 931-932ms - only the 250ms reconnection answered 'leadership lost while committing log'. Across the two runs the overlap holds in twelve of twelve trials and success in eight of twelve, so what reproduces is the overlap, while the verdict itself remains a per-trial choice between the ready verify case and the ready lease case. The account, its defect claim and its resolved gap answer are otherwise unchanged.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":cur['knowledge'],\n \\\"answers\\\":cur['answers'],\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":ce,\n \\\"limitations\\\":lim,\n \\\"joint_history\\\":cur['joint_history']+\\\" The repeat re-executed experiment 29a71a7377a44fdbac949d4808f7b847-experiment unchanged in a clean copy, so its receipt shares the harness, the timeouts, the reconnection delays and the measurement fields with the first.\\\"}\nknowledge={\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"f02f3b73bd1b44eba8471369b03da52b-knowledge-0\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":(\\\"A leader whose main loop is stalled past its lease can return VerifyLeader success while a successor already leads the cluster at a higher term, because the acknowledgement it counts arrives on a replication goroutine and the lease check that would have removed it runs on the stalled main loop. Two executions of the same probe show the overlap in twelve of twelve trials, with another server leading at term 3 from 319-511ms after the partition while the old leader stayed at term 2; eight of those twelve trials returned success at 931-932ms (three of six in the first run, five of six in the repeat) and four answered 'leadership lost while committing log'.\\\"),\n \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Three voters plus one non-voter; the leader isolated from both other voters and from the non-voter while the request is registered; the leader's main loop then blocked inside StoreLogs for 900ms by a client Apply; the non-voter reconnected 250-500ms later; HeartbeatTimeout = ElectionTimeout = LeaderLeaseTimeout = 200ms, in-memory transports in one process.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'] and [\\\"verify_leader\\\",\\\"quorum_size\\\",\\\"start_stop_repl\\\",\\\"notify_all\\\",\\\"update_last_appended\\\",\\\"verify_vote\\\",\\\"lease_check\\\",\\\"lease_check_granularity\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{ORIG:[1,3,5,7,9,11], REP:[1,3,5,7,9,11]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":(\\\"The premise is unchanged and the evidence is extended: a repeat of the same fixed probe reproduced the overlap in every trial and returned success in five of six rather than three of six, so the witness now rests on two executions. The verdict remains a per-trial choice and that is recorded rather than averaged away.\\\"),\n \\\"affected_uses\\\":[]}\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Interpreted the repeat of the witness probe. The successor overlap appeared again in all six trials, with the successor leading at term 3 from 345-511ms while the old leader stayed at term 2, and five of six trials returned VerifyLeader success at 931-932ms against three of six in the first run; only the 250ms reconnection answered leadership loss. The account therefore keeps its defect claim and its resolved gap, gains the repeat receipt in its executions, and replaces the counterevidence and limitation that spoke of a single execution with the joint figures across twelve trials, where the overlap is what reproduces and the verdict stays a per-trial choice. The Fact is extended under its own id with both receipts and the same recording of the split rather than an averaged rate. No execution is requested.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[knowledge],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
